## 1. DEPLOYMENT OVERVIEW

### 1.1 Deployment Environments

Development Environment:
  - Purpose: Local development and testing
  - Server: Local machine (Windows/Mac/Linux)
  - Database: Local database or H2
  - Access: Developer only

Testing/QA Environment:
  - Purpose: Pre-production testing
  - Server: Test server
  - Database: Test database (similar to production)
  - Access: QA team

Staging Environment:
  - Purpose: Final validation before production
  - Server: Staging server (same config as production)
  - Database: Production-like database
  - Access: Limited team members

Production Environment:
  - Purpose: Live application for end users
  - Server: Production server(s)
  - Database: Production database
  - Access: Limited admin access only

### 1.2 Deployment Strategies

Blue-Green Deployment:
  - Two identical production environments (Blue & Green)
  - Deploy to inactive environment
  - Switch traffic to new version
  - Advantage: Zero downtime, easy rollback

Rolling Deployment:
  - Gradually replace instances
  - Update 1 server at a time
  - Advantage: No downtime, gradual deployment
  - Disadvantage: Complex monitoring

Canary Deployment:
  - Deploy to small percentage of users first
  - Gradually increase traffic
  - Advantage: Risk reduction, early issue detection

Recreate Deployment:
  - Stop old version, deploy new version
  - Advantage: Simple
  - Disadvantage: Downtime required

