## 3. LOCAL DEVELOPMENT SETUP

### 3.1 Prerequisites

Software Requirements:
  - Java JDK 8+ (OpenJDK or Oracle JDK)
  - Maven 3.6+ or Gradle 6+
  - Git 2.25+
  - Docker & Docker Compose (for containerized dev)
  - PostgreSQL/MySQL (for database)
  - IDE: IntelliJ IDEA or Eclipse

Installation Steps:

1. Install Java JDK:
   Windows:
     - Download from https://adoptopenjdk.net/
     - Run installer
     - Set JAVA_HOME environment variable
     - Verify: java -version

   Linux (Ubuntu):
     sudo apt update
     sudo apt install openjdk-11-jdk
     java -version

2. Install Maven:
   Windows:
     - Download from https://maven.apache.org/
     - Extract to C:\Program Files\apache-maven
     - Add M2_HOME and PATH environment variable
     - Verify: mvn -version

   Linux:
     sudo apt install maven
     mvn -version

3. Clone Repository:
   git clone https://github.com/yourrepo/myweb.git
   cd myweb

4. Build Project:
   mvn clean install
   mvn clean package

### 3.2 Database Setup (Local)

PostgreSQL Setup:
  1. Install PostgreSQL (https://www.postgresql.org/download/)
  2. Create database:
     createdb myweb_dev
  3. Create user:
     psql -U postgres
     CREATE USER myweb_user WITH PASSWORD 'password123';
     ALTER ROLE myweb_user SET client_encoding TO 'utf8';
     ALTER ROLE myweb_user SET default_transaction_isolation TO 'read committed';
     ALTER ROLE myweb_user SET default_transaction_deferrable TO on;
     ALTER ROLE myweb_user SET timezone TO 'UTC';
     GRANT ALL PRIVILEGES ON DATABASE myweb_dev TO myweb_user;

