## 9. KUBERNETES DEPLOYMENT

### 9.1 Kubernetes Setup

Prerequisites:
  - Kubernetes cluster (minikube, EKS, GKE, AKS)
  - kubectl CLI installed
  - Docker image pushed to registry

### 9.2 Kubernetes Manifests

Deployment.yaml:
```yaml
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: myweb
spec:
  replicas: 3
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: myweb
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: myweb
    spec:
      containers:
      - name: myweb
        image: myregistry.azurecr.io/myweb:1.0.0
        ports:
        - containerPort: 8080
        env:
        - name: SPRING_DATASOURCE_URL
          valueFrom:
            secretKeyRef:
              name: myweb-secret
              key: db-url
        - name: SPRING_DATASOURCE_USERNAME
          valueFrom:
            secretKeyRef:
              name: myweb-secret
              key: db-user
        - name: SPRING_DATASOURCE_PASSWORD
          valueFrom:
            secretKeyRef:
              name: myweb-secret
              key: db-password
        resources:
          requests:
            memory: "256Mi"
            cpu: "250m"
          limits:
            memory: "512Mi"
            cpu: "500m"
        livenessProbe:
          httpGet:
            path: /api/health
            port: 8080
          initialDelaySeconds: 30
          periodSeconds: 10
        readinessProbe:
          httpGet:
            path: /api/health
            port: 8080
          initialDelaySeconds: 5
          periodSeconds: 5
```

Service.yaml:
```yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: myweb-service
spec:
  type: LoadBalancer
  selector:
    app: myweb
  ports:
  - protocol: TCP
    port: 80
    targetPort: 8080
```

### 9.3 Deploy to Kubernetes

```bash
# Create namespace
kubectl create namespace myweb

# Create secrets
kubectl create secret generic myweb-secret \
  --from-literal=db-url=jdbc:postgresql://db:5432/myweb \
  --from-literal=db-user=myweb_user \
  --from-literal=db-password=password123 \
  -n myweb

# Deploy application
kubectl apply -f deployment.yaml -n myweb
kubectl apply -f service.yaml -n myweb

# Check deployment status
kubectl get deployments -n myweb
kubectl get pods -n myweb
kubectl get services -n myweb

# View logs
kubectl logs -f deployment/myweb -n myweb

# Scale deployment
kubectl scale deployment myweb --replicas=5 -n myweb

# Update image (rolling update)
kubectl set image deployment/myweb \
  myweb=myregistry.azurecr.io/myweb:1.0.1 -n myweb
```

