## 12. ROLLBACK PROCEDURES

### 12.1 Immediate Rollback (First 30 minutes)

If Critical Issues Detected:
  1. Alert team immediately
  2. Identify issue (logs, metrics)
  3. Decide rollback vs fix forward

### 12.2 Rollback to Previous Version

Tomcat Rollback:
```bash
# Stop application
/opt/tomcat/bin/shutdown.sh

# Restore previous WAR file
cp /backup/myweb-20260513-100000.war /opt/tomcat/webapps/myweb.war

# Start application
/opt/tomcat/bin/startup.sh

# Verify
curl https://prod.example.com/api/health
```

systemd Service Rollback:
```bash
# Stop application
sudo systemctl stop myweb

# Restore previous JAR
cp /backup/myweb-1.0.0.jar /opt/myweb/app/

# Start application
sudo systemctl start myweb

# Verify
sudo systemctl status myweb
```

Kubernetes Rollback:
```bash
# View rollout history
kubectl rollout history deployment/myweb -n myweb

# Rollback to previous version
kubectl rollout undo deployment/myweb -n myweb

# Rollback to specific revision
kubectl rollout undo deployment/myweb --to-revision=2 -n myweb

# Verify rollback
kubectl get pods -n myweb
```

### 12.3 Database Rollback

If Database Schema Changes:
```bash
# Restore from backup
psql -U myweb_user myweb < /backup/myweb-db-20260513-100000.sql

# Or use Flyway/Liquibase rollback
mvn flyway:undo
```

